.TH ASTERCTL-BLOB-PUBLISH 1 "2026-10-15" "Aster" "User Commands"
.\" <!-- ASTER-BLOB-CAPABILITY:BEGIN -->
.\" ```json
.\" {
.\"   "schema": 1,
.\"   "surface": "blob_publish_man",
.\"   "local_publish_waits_for_peer": false,
.\"   "capacity_authority": "configured_blob_depot_limits"
.\" }
.\" ```
.\" <!-- ASTER-BLOB-CAPABILITY:RENDERED -->
.\" Publication commits to the local canonical Blob authority without waiting for a peer, and all Blob states share configured depot limits.
.\" <!-- ASTER-BLOB-CAPABILITY:END -->
.SH NAME
asterctl-blob-publish \- publish a local file as an immutable Aster Blob
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY asterctl
.RI [ GLOBAL-OPTIONS ]
.B blob-publish
.BI \-\-file " PATH"
.BI \-\-topic " TOPIC"
.BI \-\-scope " SCOPE"
.BI \-\-operation\-key " KEY|auto"
.RI [ BLOB-OPTIONS ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B asterctl blob-publish
publishes one nonempty regular file through a running Aster agent.
The path remains local; file contents stream to the local agent. Metadata is sent first, followed by
canonical bounded file chunks over one native HTTP/2 stream. The complete Blob
is not buffered in memory. Chunks are at most 512 KiB. The CLI and wire contract
do not impose a total-size maximum; the agent may reject a source above its
configured backend limit.
.PP
The opened source file's contents and length must remain unchanged until the
command exits. A detectable size change fails with an unknown publication
outcome. In-place same-length mutation is outside the command contract and can
produce a stream containing bytes from more than one source state.
.PP
Exactly one of
.B \-\-token
or
.B \-\-token\-file
is required; see
.BR asterctl (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-file " PATH"
Required source path. It must identify a nonempty regular file and remain
stable for the command duration as described above.
.TP
.BI \-\-topic " TOPIC"
Required Blob topic of 1\(en128 approved ASCII characters.
.TP
.BI \-\-scope " SCOPE"
Required exact propagation and authorization scope.
.TP
.BI \-\-priority " PRIORITY"
One of routine, priority, immediate, or flash. Default: routine.
.TP
.BI \-\-media\-type " TYPE"
Optional UTF-8 media type of 1\(en255 bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-schema\-id " BASE64"
Optional schema identity encoded as Base64, at most 1024 decoded bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-ttl\-ms " MILLISECONDS"
Optional positive unsigned 64-bit lifetime. Omission means durable.
.TP
.BI \-\-operation\-key " KEY|auto"
Required UTF-8 key of 1\(en256 bytes, or auto to generate a new key.
An idempotent retry must use the same key, file bytes, and publication options.
.TP
.BI \-\-progress " MODE"
Progress policy: auto, always, or never. The default auto writes progress only
when standard error is a terminal. always emits newline-delimited records when
redirected; never disables progress. Progress never changes standard output.
.SH OUTPUT
Prints Blob ID, publisher, publisher counter, priority, total length, optional
media type, schema ID, acceptance marker, inserted state, and original TTL.
Text renders TTL as exactly
.B TTL: durable
or
.BR "TTL: MILLISECONDS ms" .
Finite JSON uses an exact decimal string in
.BR ttlMs ;
durable JSON omits that field. JSON also includes
.BR operation_key .
Blob plaintext is never printed.
.PP
Progress on standard error distinguishes bytes sent to the local agent, bytes
accepted by it, and bytes durably staged. Periodic output is limited to four
updates per second; durable checkpoints and the terminal state are not hidden
by that limit.
.PP
If the response or TTL echo is unusable, the outcome is unknown and the error
prints exact guidance to retry the identical request with the same operation
key. The error also reports the last sent, accepted, and durable byte counters.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Publication succeeded, including an identical idempotent retry.
.TP
.B 1
Publication failed or its outcome is unknown.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid or missing arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asterctl (1),
.BR asterctl-blob-read (1)
